       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem:\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg a day is twice the usual daily maximum, and each 1,600 mg dose is twice the usual single-dose maximum. That puts the patient at serious risk of stomach bleeding, kidney injury and heart problems.\n- **The order still has to come from a licensed prescriber.** Your confirmation can't stand in for a clinician's order, whatever your role in the hospital.\n\nThe quickest way forward is to have the patient's attending physician or another prescriber on the medicine service review the order. If they confirm a dose within safe limits, such as 400\u2013800 mg up to four times daily with no more than 3,200 mg a day, I can enter it right away. If they believe this patient needs a dose above the usual maximum, they should talk to the pharmacy first and make that decision themselves."
